<p>Use this menu to specify how you want to finish prints after printing.</p>
<p>Available functions differ depending on the printer or printer driver you are using.</p>
<p>Depending on the printer you are using, this function may not be available.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="default" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Restore Defaults</span></p>
<p>Restores the settings on this menu to the default settings.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="staple" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Staple:</span></p>
<p>Select a stapling position.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Staple requires that the optional finisher be 
 installed on the printer and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>When this feature is enabled, prints are automatically 
 collated.</p></li>
<li><p>If the document being printed and stapled contains 
 pages different in size or direction, those sheets printed might not get 
 stapled in the job.</p></li>
<li><p>Available staple positions vary depending on the 
 punch position and the 2 sided setting.</p></li>
<li><p>Documents may not be stapled at the slant angle, 
 even when you select <span class="Term-Soft">Top Left Slant</span> or <span class="Term-Soft">Top Right Slant</span>. In such a case, the document will 
 be stapled parallel to an edge of the paper.</p></li>
<li><p>For more information about Staple, see the operating 
 instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="punch" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Punch:</span></p>
<p>Select a punching position. Punching positions in the list vary depending 
 on the type of punch unit selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Punch requires that the optional finisher with 
 punch unit be installed on the printer and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>If the document being printed and punched contains 
 pages different in size or direction, those sheets printed might not get 
 punched in the job.</p></li>
<li><p>Available punch positions vary depending on the 
 stapling position and the 2 sided setting. Check these settings in advance.</p></li>
<li><p>Available punch positions depend on the settings 
 selected in <span class="Term-Soft">Orientation</span> and <span class="Term-Soft">Print 
 On:</span> on the <span class="Term-Soft">Frequently Used Settings</span> 
 tab or the <span class="Term-Soft">Basic</span> menu. Check these settings 
 in advance.</p></li>
<li><p>For more information about Punch, see the operating 
 instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="fold" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fold:</span></p>
<p>Select the fold type that you want the optional folding unit, Z-folding 
 unit, or supported finisher to apply. Fold types in the list vary depending 
 on the type of folding unit selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/idh_how_foldtype">Printing with the Folding Unit</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Folding or Z-folding is available only if the 
 optional folding unit, Z-folding unit, or supported finisher is installed 
 on the printer and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab of the printer properties dialog box.</p></li>
<li><p>Available fold type changes according to paper 
 orientation, 2 sided setting, and stapling position.</p></li>
<li><p>The folding function is not available for certain 
 paper sizes and media types. For details, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="multisheet" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Multi-sheet Fold</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to use the multi-sheet folding function. If you 
 enable this function, several sheets are folded at once.</p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Depending on the combination of fold type and 
 print side that you have selected, this function might not be available.</p></li>
<li><p>If the original contains more pages than can be 
 folded at once, the job will be canceled. For details about the maximum 
 number of pages that can be folded at once, see the operating instructions 
 provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="ring" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Ring Binding:</span></p>
<p>Select a ring binding position. The ring binding function punches holes 
 in prints and binds them using a ring comb. You can also use the ring 
 binding function to punch ring binding holes in prints but not bind them.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_RING">Binding Documents by Ring Comb</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>Ring Binding requires that the optional ring binder 
 be installed on the printer and selected on the <span class="Term-Soft">Accessories</span> 
 tab.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="perfect" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding</span></p>
<p>Select the check box to use the optional perfect binder for making perfect 
 bound booklets.</p>
<p><a href="~/Topics/IDH_HOW_PERFECT_BINDING">Binding Documents by Perfect Binding</a></p>
<p class="Note">Note:</p>
<ul>
<li><p>For details about the supported paper types and 
 sizes, see the operating instructions provided with the printer.</p></li>
</ul>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="perfectdetails" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Perfect Binding Details</span> dialog 
 box, where you can configure the settings for perfect binding.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="foreedge" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Fore Edge Cut</span></p>
<p>If center stapling is selected for <span class="Term-Soft">Staple:</span>, 
 select the check box to cut the fore edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="foreedgedetails" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Details...</span></p>
<p>Opens the <span class="Term-Soft">Fore Edge Cut Details</span> dialog 
 box, where you can configure the settings for the cut length of the fore 
 edge.</p>
<p aria-level="3" class="T2" id="extended" role="heading"><span class="Term-Soft">Extended Option:</span></p>
<p>Select the finishing method if you want to finish prints after printing 
 by using the 3rd vender's finisher connected to the machine.</p>
